  "query_preview": "..\n\nAn upper-level ridge over the western US will result in high \ntemperatures that are 5 to 15 degrees above normal and relatively \ndry conditions today. If fires were to develop nearby, the HRRR \nand RAP anticipate smoke potentially producing light haze in our \nregion. \n\nThe ridge will gradually decay as the week progresses and an \nupper-level low and its associated trough exit the Aleutian \nregion and dig over the PNW. The weakening ridge will result in \ntemperatures decreasing marginally through Thursday. A slight \nrebound in temperatures will occur Friday as the weakened ridge \ncrests over NE Montana.\n\nThe warmth will not last. The ridge will quickly exit eastward\nFriday night as the aforementioned PNW low digs as far as Point\nConception between Saturday and Monday mornings. The subsequent\namplified trough will produce strong cold air and moisture \nadvection into the CWA behind an approaching front. Overcast \nskies, possible precipitation, and low temperatures anticipated \nthis weekend and into Monday.\n\nPrecipitation chances begin late Saturday with rain showers as \ndaily high temperatures decrease and winds increase significantly\nbehind frontal passage. Temperatures will continue diving into \nSunday, with highs in the 40s, nearly 20 degrees below normal. \nSnow may be possible overnight Sunday. If snow occurs, totals are \nanticipated to be less than an inch; melt will occur quickly.\n\nCooler and wetter conditions are expected to persist through \nMonday before beginning beginning to rebound Tuesday. However, \nforecasts beyond Saturday become less certain due to ensemble \ninconsistencies. Additionally, model guidance suggests the upper-\nlevel ridge to the east will become quasi-stationary, potentially\nstalling trough propagation. This may result in cooler/wetter\nconditions lasting longer than currently expected. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- No changes from NBM.\n\n- There is moderate to low confidence (30-50%) in frontal timing\n  Friday night/Saturday morning.\n\n- There is high confidence (70-90%) in warmer temperatures through\n  Friday and cooler temperatures this weekend.\n\n- There is moderate to high confidence (50-80%) in any\n  precipitation occuring between Saturday night and Monday\n  morning.",
